  "fields": {
    "title": "SVG ",
    "textContent": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Description",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "SVG, short for Scalable Vector Graphic, defines vector-based 2D graphics in XML, which can be directly embedded in Websites. SVG graphics are scalable, and do not lose any quality if they are zoomed or resized. You can attach JavaScript event handlers to SVG graphics and animate each element and attribute in SVG files using. SVG is, essentially, to graphics what ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "5E1SmovXET5h0cV1E0tOzT",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "HTML",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " is to text. ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Background",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "In the early days of the Web, there was an explosion of different formats and extensions to HTML. From early on, it was clear that a vector graphic format for the Web would be useful. Chris Lilley wrote up a document for ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://www.w3.org/Graphics/ScalableReq.html"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "general requirements for vector graphics",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " in 1996. In 1998 SVG WG was chartered by the W3 consortium. Over the course of SVG's development, the strongest early influences were W3C's Chris Lilley and Adobe's Jon Ferraiolo.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "superscript"
                }
              ],
              "value": "[1]",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Possibilities",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Applications such as Adobe Illustrator or Figma have the possibility to export graphics as SVG files. This is a easy way to create a SVG without having to code it from scratch.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The SVG file format offers some great features. Here are some examples:",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "SVG Filter: These can be applied to SVGs but also to images. They offer a variety of effects, such as G",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ],
                      "value": "aussian Blur",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": " or ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ],
                      "value": "Displacement Maps",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": ". Some of these effects are similar to After Effects and Photoshop effects. If you wanna play around with them, have a look at this ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {
                        "uri": "https://yoksel.github.io/svg-filters/#/"
                      },
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "data": {},
                          "marks": [],
                          "value": "SVG Filter Tester",
                          "nodeType": "text"
                        }
                      ],
                      "nodeType": "hyperlink"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": ". And if you are curious how SVG filter could be used on a website, take a look at ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {
                        "uri": "https://simulacrum247.dervierteraum.org/"
                      },
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "data": {},
                          "marks": [],
                          "value": "this site",
                          "nodeType": "text"
                        }
                      ],
                      "nodeType": "hyperlink"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": ".",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "Animation: There are different ways to animate a SVG. One is using SMIL, short for Synchronized Multimedia Integration Language, which is an XML-based language for writing interactive multimedia presentations. SMIL allows you to animate the numeric attributes of an element (x, y, etc), transform attributes (translation, rotate, etc), change colors or following a motion path. Another way to animate a SVG is using CSS ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {
                        "target": {
                          "sys": {
                            "id": "61aVmYIGxb3YW3gRUMKoVs",
                            "type": "Link",
                            "linkType": "Entry"
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "data": {},
                          "marks": [],
                          "value": "Keyframe Animation",
                          "nodeType": "text"
                        }
                      ],
                      "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": ", which can be applied by using for example class-names inside a SVG. ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "Clipping and masking: You can clip and mask forms inside a SVG. This works similar to to the pathfinder tool in Adobe Illustrator and can be quite useful for a variety of cases. As you can also embed images inside a SVG, masking can for example be used to show images inside a unusual shape. ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "Gradient and pattern: SVGs have some powerful fill types like patterns and gradients. You can create and apply gradients as either fills or strokes and there are two types of SVG gradients: linear and radial.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "unordered-list"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Example",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Here you can see a simple example of text animated on a motion path:",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "nodeType": "document"
    },
    "codeField": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ],
              "value": "html\n<!-- example code of a svg animation -->\n<svg\n    class=\"example_svg_animation\"\n    width=\"100%\"\n    height=\"75px\"\n    viewBox=\"0 0 380 60\"\n    preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin\"\n>\n    <path\n        id=\"rect-large\"\n        fill=\"transparent\"\n        d=\"M14,10h332a4,4 0 0 1 4,4v32a4,4 0 0 1 -4,4h-332a-4,-4 0 0 1 -4,-4v-32a4,-4 0 0 1 4,-4z\"\n    ></path>\n    <path\n        id=\"rect-small\"\n        fill=\"transparent\"\n        d=\"M25,24h310a1,1 0 0 1 1,1v10a1,1 0 0 1 -1,1h-310a-1,-1 0 0 1 -1,-1v-10a1,-1 0 0 1 1,-1z\"\n    ></path>\n    <text width=\"100%\">\n        <textPath alignment-baseline=\"top\" href=\"#rect-large\">\n            <animate\n                attributeName=\"startOffset\"\n                from=\"0%\"\n                to=\"100%\"\n                begin=\"0s\"\n                dur=\"12s\"\n                repeatCount=\"indefinite\"\n            ></animate> Coding a website doesn't have to be hard, but can\n            be soft and fun. </textPath>\n        <textPath alignment-baseline=\"top\" href=\"#rect-large\">\n            <animate\n                attributeName=\"startOffset\"\n                from=\"-100%\"\n                to=\"0%\"\n                begin=\"0s\"\n                dur=\"12s\"\n                repeatCount=\"indefinite\"\n            ></animate> Coding a website doesn't have to be hard, but can\n            be soft and fun. </textPath>\n    </text>\n    <text width=\"100%\">\n        <textPath alignment-baseline=\"top\" href=\"#rect-small\">\n            <animate\n                attributeName=\"startOffset\"\n                from=\"100%\"\n                to=\"0%\"\n                begin=\"0s\"\n                dur=\"10s\"\n                repeatCount=\"indefinite\"\n            ></animate> Coding a website doesn't have to be hard, but can\n            be soft and fun. </textPath>\n        <textPath alignment-baseline=\"top\" href=\"#rect-small\">\n            <animate\n                attributeName=\"startOffset\"\n                from=\"0%\"\n                to=\"-100%\"\n                begin=\"0s\"\n                dur=\"10s\"\n                repeatCount=\"indefinite\"\n            ></animate> Coding a website doesn't have to be hard, but can\n            be soft and fun. </textPath>\n    </text>\n</svg>",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "nodeType": "document"
    },
